.TH BOBSHIT 1 "2026" "BobShit 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bobshit \- run a BobShit program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bobshit
.RI [ options ]
.IR file.shit
.br
.B bobshit run
.I file.shit
.br
.B bobshit \-e
.I code
.br
.B bobshit \-i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bobshit
is the reference interpreter of BobShit, a soft, human-first interpreted
language. It runs a
.I .shit
source file, a snippet of code, or an interactive session.
.PP
By default BobShit runs in
.B soft
mode: missing parentheses, missing
.BR end ,
missing commas, unterminated strings and stray characters are absorbed with
a warning instead of aborting. Pass
.B \-s
to turn those warnings into hard errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "run " file.shit
Explicit spelling of the default action.
.TP
.BI "\-e " code " | " \-\-eval " code
Evaluate
.I code
instead of a file.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Start the REPL. Multi-line blocks and multi-line lists are read until they are
balanced.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-strict
Disable soft mode. The first diagnostic aborts the program with exit code 1.
.TP
.B \-\-soft
Force soft mode (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-hold
Wait for Enter before exiting. Used by the Windows file association so that
double clicking a
.I .shit
file does not close the console before the output can be read.
.TP
.B \-\-ast
Print the AST of the input and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tokens
Print the token stream of the input and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B bobshit hello.shit
Run a script.
.TP
.B bobshit \-e 'say "hi", 1+1'
Run a one liner.
.TP
.B echo 'say "salut"' > x.shit && chmod +x x.shit && ./x.shit
Run a script through its shebang, with
.B #!/usr/bin/env bobshit
as its first line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program ran to completion.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error was not caught, the first strict-mode diagnostic was hit, or
the file could not be read.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/bobshit/LANGUAGE.md
The full language reference: lexique, types, collections, control flow,
functions, builtins, grammar and recipes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/bobshit/examples/
Runnable examples, also served as executable documentation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Soft mode emits warnings on standard error and the CLI prints a one line
summary of the warning count at the end of the run.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full language reference ships in
.IR /usr/share/doc/bobshit/LANGUAGE.md .
.SH BUGS
No garbage collector: memory used by values is not reclaimed before the
process exits. The call stack is capped at 256 frames and each loop statement
at 1,000,000 iterations.
